<div class="section-width--thin">
  <h2>[ Hero Image Circle - Section ]</h2>
  <br />
  <p>
    A hero with circular image cluster(s) (built on the
    <code>image-circle</code> component) flanking or overflowing alongside the
    title/description/CTAs. Takes:
  </p>
  <br />
  <ul class="classic-list">
    <li>
      <code>pre_image</code> an optional image ( <code>src</code> /
      <code>alt</code> ) shown above the title. Leave <code>src</code> unset to
      hide it.
    </li>
    <li><code>title</code> and <code>description</code> strings.</li>
    <li>
      <code>cta_1</code> / <code>cta_2</code> same shape as the
      <code>cta-group</code> component.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>images_1</code> / <code>images_2</code> each an array of images (
      <code>src</code> / <code>alt</code> ) for the two image clusters.
      <code>images_2</code> is ignored when <code>direction</code> is
      <code>left</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>direction</code> a string, <code>center</code> or <code>left</code>.
      <code>center</code> (default) flanks the content with both circles.
      <code>left</code> drops the second circle, shifts the copy to the left,
      and lets the first circle overflow off the right edge of the screen.
      Desktop (<code>lg</code> and up) only — mobile looks identical either way.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>images_scrub</code> a number, <code>0</code> (default) is off. Spins
      each circle as the user scrolls while the section is in the viewport;
      <code>1</code> is roughly a quarter turn across the section's full pass
      through the viewport, so higher values rotate more dramatically. With two
      circles they spin in opposite directions, matching their idle spin.
      Skipped when the user prefers reduced motion.
    </li>
  </ul>
</div>
<!-- prettier-ignore -->
