<div class="section-width--thin">
  <h2>[ Hero Image Wave - Section ]</h2>
  <br />
  <p>
    A hero that's always a centered column, with an accent flourish and an
    <code>image-wave</code> component beneath the content. Takes:
  </p>
  <br />
  <ul class="classic-list">
    <li><code>eyebrow</code> an optional string shown above the title.</li>
    <li><code>title</code> and <code>description</code> strings.</li>
    <li>
      <code>accent</code> an optional string, decorative text positioned
      absolutely beside the copy. Hidden on mobile (<code>lg</code> and down).
      Leave unset to omit.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>cta_1</code> / <code>cta_2</code> same shape as the
      <code>cta-group</code> component.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>images</code> an array of images ( <code>src</code> /
      <code>alt</code> ) passed to the <code>image-wave</code> component.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>wave</code> an optional object of <code>image-wave</code> configs —
      <code>repeat</code>, <code>speed</code>, <code>duration</code>,
      <code>amplitude</code>, <code>waves</code>, <code>scrub</code>,
      <code>class</code>. See the component's docs for what each does.
    </li>
  </ul>
</div>
<!-- prettier-ignore -->
{% set hero_image_wave = library.sections.hero_image_wave %}
{% include '../_includes/sections/hero-image-wave.njk' %}

<div class="section-width--thin">
  <h2>[ Headline - Section ]</h2>
  <br />
  <p>
    A centered statement that flips in word by word (the
    <code>text-flip</code> util), with an optional eyebrow and, if given a quote
    giver, wrapped in quotes and credited beneath. It's a <code>p</code> rather
    than an <code>h2</code>, as it's a statement, not a section title. Takes:
  </p>
  <br />
  <ul class="classic-list">
    <li>
      <code>text</code> a string, the headline. 'Safe' for markup, so
      <code>em</code> / <code>strong</code> accents work.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>eyebrow</code> an optional string shown above the headline, via the
      <code>eyebrow</code> component.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>icon</code> an optional string, the path to an svg shown before the
      eyebrow. Works without <code>eyebrow</code> text too.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>quote_giver</code> an object of <code>name</code>,
      <code>role</code> and <code>image</code> ( <code>src</code> /
      <code>alt</code> ). These fields are always available: leave
      <code>name</code> empty and the headline stays plain, with no quotes. Give
      it a <code>name</code> and the headline is wrapped in quotes, with the
      giver's image, name and role beneath.
    </li>
    <li><code>class</code> a string value for a custom css class.</li>
  </ul>
</div>
